---
/**
 * The studio floor: one fixed layer behind the whole page. A plane in true CSS perspective carries
 * a 64px grid that fades toward the horizon at 58% of the viewport; the horizon glow crossfades
 * between six colours as `client.ts` sets `data-stage` on <html>.
 *
 * The scene's perspective origin sits 744px below the horizon: with `perspective: 1400px` and a
 * plane tilted 62°, that is where the grid lines converge, so the floor reads as flat ground and the
 * fade lands exactly on its vanishing line. The hero's billboards use the same geometry.
 */
---

<div class="ky-floor" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="ky-floor__scene">
    <div class="ky-floor__plane"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ky-floor__flat"></div>
  <i class="ky-glow ky-glow--teal"></i>
  <i class="ky-glow ky-glow--green"></i>
  <i class="ky-glow ky-glow--blue"></i>
  <i class="ky-glow ky-glow--violet"></i>
  <i class="ky-glow ky-glow--red"></i>
  <i class="ky-glow ky-glow--gold"></i>
  <i class="ky-horizon"></i>
</div>
